a. Each DFSH will include all flights that departed on the previous calendar day (local departure
  time) for that specific fleet of aircraft (e.g. B717, A321, A330, B787)

  3. Further, the DFSH will include the following:
  a. Date;
  b. Type of Equipment;
  c. Flight Number;
  d. Each pilot assigned to Flight Grouping(s) to which assigned;
  e. Names of all pilot and their respective positions;
  f. Names of all pilots “Deadheading” under Company orders;
  g. The time of arrival for all Segments
  h. How the Flight Grouping was assigned:
  1) Bid Run
  2) Reserve (LCR, Short Call)
  3) OV75
  4) Recall
  5) Reassignment
  i. Changes made pursuant to the provisions of:
  1) Subsection 4.D (Pay and Credit for Schedule Changes);
  2) Subsection 21.J (Modification of Awards).

  4. The Daily Flight Schedule History will be posted not later than 1800 LDT (Local Domicile Time) on
  the day following the day on which the schedule was flown. For the purposes of this Subparagraph
  22.K.4, “posting” shall mean the distribution through e-mail copy to:

  a. Hawaiian Airlines Pilot’s Flight Crew Information System (ALPA electronic bulletin board);
  b. MEC Office;
  c. Hawaiian Airlines Flight Division Website.

  5. The DFSH shall be available for printout by individual pilots.

